<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  BELLUM CIVILE - Feudal Title Configuration

  This file can predefine de jure title hierarchy at game start.
  References may use stable IDs or display names:
    settlement="town_V1" or settlement="Sargot"
    deJureClan="clan_vlandia_1" or deJureClan="dey Meroc"
    kingdom="vlandia" or kingdom="Vlandia"

  Title names are territorial roots, not full rendered legal names.
  If name is omitted, Bellum uses the title capital/settlement root:
    Sargot
    Talivel
    Jaculan

  The displayed legal title is assembled from the holder's title style:
    Vlandian style + root "Jaculan" => County of Jaculan
    Nord style + root "Jaculan" => Chiefdom of Jaculan, if configured that way

  Special names can be configured directly on a title:
    name="the Tall Hills"
  A Vlandian count holding it would then be styled as:
    Count of the Tall Hills, ruling the County of the Tall Hills.

  TitleStyle defines cultural, ruler-cultural, or kingdom-specific landed
  nouns, personal ranks, and optional formatting. Resolution order is:
    kingdom="vlandia"       => exact institutional realm style
    rulerCulture="Vlandia" => every clan follows its realm ruler's culture
    culture="Vlandia"      => the individual holder's own culture
  Kingdomless holders retain their own cultural style instead of borrowing
  terminology from a captured title's historical realm.
  These fields can use localization IDs, for example
  maleRank="{=BC_TitleDisplay_King}King".

  Optional per-rank formats:
    titleFormat="{TITLE_NOUN} of {TITLE_NAME}"   => County of Jaculan
    titleFormat="{TITLE_NAME} {TITLE_NOUN}"      => Jaculan County
    heldTitleFormat="{DISPLAY_TITLE} of {TITLE_NAME}" => Count of Jaculan
    heldTitleFormat="{TITLE_NAME} {TITLE_RANK}"       => Jaculan Count
    heroNameFormat="{DISPLAY_TITLE} {HERO_NAME}"      => Count Derthert
    heroNameFormat="{HERO_NAME} {DISPLAY_TITLE}"      => Derthert Count
    heroNameFormat="{HERO_NAME}, {HELD_TITLE}"         => Derthert, Count of Jaculan
    heroNameFormat="{DISPLAY_TITLE} &#xB7; {HERO_NAME}" => Count · Derthert

  Recruited wanderers are retainers rather than nobles and receive no
  honorific by default. A culture or kingdom may style them explicitly:
    wandererRank="Retainer" femaleWandererRank="Retainer"

  Vacant titles are supported by omitting deJureClan/deFactoClan.

  Optional honorifics for noble clan leaders with no active de facto title:
    landlessLeaderRank="Patriarch" femaleLandlessLeaderRank="Matriarch"
  Set these on the realm's sovereign Rank tier (Kingdom or Empire normally).
  They follow the generic noble style's own-culture preference, then realm
  fallbacks. Omitted values preserve nobleRank/femaleNobleRank behavior; a
  single supplied gender serves both. Ordinary members and leaders holding
  any title are unaffected. Royal, heir and consort styles take priority.
  The realm-membership, adulthood and non-mercenary noble requirements remain.

  Optional mercenary/minor-faction clan leader honorifics on Rank tier="Kingdom":
    mercenaryLeaderRank="Captain" femaleMercenaryLeaderRank="Captain"
  Own-culture entries work both hired and between contracts; realm styles are
  fallbacks. Includes the player while serving as a mercenary. Adult leaders
  only, excluding bandits/notables; never inherited by members or spouses.
  Omit both to retain existing names. One gender can serve both. These are
  professional honorifics, not territorial ranks, and take priority while eligible.
-->
